{"name":"Dark Rift","hex":"#060b14","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"rift","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chasm or fissure.","A lack of cohesion; a state of conflict, incompatibility, or emotional distance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a rift; to split open.","To cleave; to rive; to split."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rift"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark Rift","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Rift is a 1997 fighting video game developed by Kronos Digital Entertainment and published by Vic Tokai for the Nintendo 64 and Microsoft Windows. It is notable for being the first N64 game to run at 60 frames per second."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/84/Darkrift.jpg/330px-Darkrift.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Rift"},{"title":"Dark Rift (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Rift is a studio album by American electronic musician Pictureplane. It was released by Lovepump United Records on August 4, 2009. Music videos were created for \"Trance Doll\" and \"Goth Star\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/Dark_Rift_-_Pictureplane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Rift_(album)"},{"title":"Rift","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rift is a linear zone where the lithosphere is being pulled apart and is an example of extensional tectonics. Typical rift features are a central linear downfaulted depression, called a graben, or more commonly a half-graben with normal faulting and rift-flank uplifts mainly on one side. Where rifts remain above sea level they form a rift valley, which may be filled by water forming a rift lake. The axis of the rift area may contain volcanic rocks, and active volcanism is a part of many, but not all, active rift systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Rift_segmentation.png/330px-Rift_segmentation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rift"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Dark_Rift_gameplay.jpg/250px-Dark_Rift_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9c/Dark_Rift_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Dark_Rift_gameplay.jpg/250px-Dark_Rift_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gameplay screenshot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADark_Rift_gameplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/1280px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut